From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downloads: finish chapters with fewer SAF copies and show why
 a download failed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port of anikku-harmony 0016 to the manga downloader. On providers without
renameDocument (HarmonyOS ZhuoyiTong's SAF bridge) the 0001 fallback copied the
whole chapter directory page by page and any failure after the progress bar hit
100% was invisible: isDownloadSuccessful() == false set ERROR without a message,
notification or log line, and error notifications are not shown inside 卓易通.

- UniFileExtensions.renameToOrCopy(targetName, resolver): byte-identical to the
  Anikku copy. For directories, try DocumentsContract.moveDocument per child
  first (metadata move on providers that support it), fall back to copying, merge
  into an existing target directory left by an interrupted attempt (same-size
  files are kept), verify copied sizes, and keep the copy when the stale source
  cannot be deleted. Unit tests updated for the new semantics (8 tests).
- Downloader: the final chapter directory rename goes through
  retryStorageOperation (3 attempts, 2 s / 4 s). When the chapter is not
  complete the reason is now recorded: "N page(s) failed to download, e.g. page
  X: <error>" when pages errored, otherwise the unexpected folder contents.
  stop() marks interrupted downloads with a readable reason; every other error
  path records its message too.
- Download.error + fail(message); DownloadHolder shows "Error" in the progress
  column and "Error: <reason>" under the chapter name (up to 3 lines);
  DownloadQueueViewModel refreshes the row when a download enters ERROR.
- Strings harmony_download_unexpected_files / harmony_download_pages_failed /
  harmony_download_error_prefix / harmony_download_interrupted in i18n base,
  zh-rCN and zh-rTW.

Per-page .tmp -> .<ext> renames are unchanged: the extension is only known after
the response, and pages are small. Animeko is not affected (no SAF).
